{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/701225-beats-per-session","id":701225,"title":"Beats per session?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-14T12:49:30-07:00","id":701225,"title":"Beats per session?","content":"Hey, I've a question for you Storytellers and players out there... How many Beats does a player accumulate in an average session in your game?<br /> Mine have been getting about 3-4 Beats per 4-hour session. Some are new players, and they're playing neonates thrust into the unlife without warning or support, so I'm making these early nights (it is currently the fourth night) played in extra high definition; with each feeding or contact with another Kindred or even obtaining new clothes getting its own scene. I think this is somewhat slowing down the attainment of Beats.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:05:33-07:00","id":701259,"title":"","content":"It depends largely on the players' own performance for me.<br /> <br /> Usually, though, there's a minimum 1 beat for the session itself, another for good RP, character development, or ideas in line with the story (and if at least one person accomplishes one of these, then I award it to everyone).<br /> <br /> So, that's a minimum of 2 beats per session.<br /> <br /> Usually more beats come in based on a lot of the suggested reasons to award them, but the ones that have come up most often are through fulfilling or working toward Aspirations (which can net you 1 to 3 beats depending), pushing a Breaking Point, choosing to let a failure become Dramatic, or a Diceless Feeding scene.<br /> <br /> Admittedly, it takes a skilled player familiar with the game rules and someone who's handy at roleplaying their character well, combined, to maximize Beats\u2014I think the most I ended up with one night was 8, for hitting all marks. (I or the other ST also award a Beat or two if someone does any game-based writing in between sessions that adds to the story or character.)<br /> <br /> On average, though, 3\u20134 beats does seem to be about the right amount per session.<br /> <br /> When there have been long gaps in a story, we've also awarded just a few Beats (for, say, a 10 year quiet period in the characters' story) since the regular sessions are basically about the amount of drama happening in a night to night basis, and the periods we skim over or 'montage' our way through are overall less intensive and dramatic (and thus less cause to award anything).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#000080\">&quot;There is the world of light, and the world of darkness. And some in the light prefer the darkness.&quot; \u2014 Loren Eiseley, <i>The Night Country</i></span>","edited":{"userid":583,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","user":"Zsander","date":". 10-14-2015, 04:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/583-zsander","name":"Zsander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar583_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"170"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:37:33-07:00","id":701275,"title":"","content":"My players usually make about 4 Beats each per session. Maybe 5 on a good night or 3 on a slow night. When I get a chance to play, I usually earn a bit more than that, but I intentionally try to milk all the Beats I can, starting play with Persistent Cobditions, favoring abilities that reliably get me Conditions, and accepting a lot of Dramatic Failures a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T13:59:08-07:00","id":701280,"title":"","content":"My players get 3-5 beats per session, but I allow multiple conditions to be resolved in the same scene.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Glorious Useless-Post Prana<br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Cost: 2</span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">m; </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mins: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Linguistics 1, Essence 1 </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Type: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Simple</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Keywords: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Mute</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Duration: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Instant</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Prerequisite Charms: </span><span style=\"font-family:MercuryTextG2\">Ten-Characters Methodology</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2589-magnum-opus","name":"Magnum Opus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2589_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"821"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T14:36:47-07:00","id":701299,"title":"","content":"We used to get 3-4, we started factoring in Exceptional Successes leading to Conditions and the average upped to 4-5, closer to five.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-14T15:42:34-07:00","id":701348,"title":"","content":"In the Werewolf game I'm in right now, we're doing pack/group beats, and we've been getting about 3-5 a session. When I ran Vampire last year, my players earned about the same, with a bit of a jump for the one character who decided to become a diablerist (you get a lot of experience for falling down the Humanity ladder). We weren't doing group beats, but it ended up averaging out, more or less.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, when I ran Demon, they were earning at least an EXP a session.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T01:51:34-07:00","id":701849,"title":"","content":"Really happy to hear that most of you are in the 3-5 range, I was getting worried that I was doing something wrong.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T04:10:41-07:00","id":701933,"title":"","content":"In my Hunter campaign, players usually earn somewhere between 4-9 normal Beats per character during the session (we use collective Beats), depending how much action, fulfilled Aspirations and Dramatic Failures is included. Beats from wounds are quite common if the cell goes to battle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","user":"Crazy_Ivan","date":". 10-15-2015, 07:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T05:06:19-07:00","id":701994,"title":"","content":"NINE!? Wow. That seems like a lot! We had one session with 5 Beats. This involved a fight, a few failed feeding rolls, a close encounter with a mentally unstable retired LtCol of the USMC, and two condition resolutions. How often do you have a fight, Ivan?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MAKE LOVE, NOT SPAM!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1956-the-boz","name":"The Boz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1956_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"132"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T06:10:48-07:00","id":702019,"title":"","content":"Mathematically, a 2e Beat has basically the same buying power as one 1e experience point, and 1e recommended giving out 3-5 exp per session, so there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-15T06:12:13-07:00","id":702022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Boz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/701225-beats-per-session?p=701994#post701994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">NINE!? Wow. That seems like a lot! We had one session with 5 Beats. This involved a fight, a few failed feeding rolls, a close encounter with a mentally unstable retired LtCol of the USMC, and two condition resolutions. How often do you have a fight, Ivan?</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite often, propably 75 % of sessions include light combat at least. I run sandboxy game with many monsters-of-the-week in the mix, and Hunters have their job cut out for them. Conditions from Expectional Successess and voluntary Dramatic Failures are common, and I usually have about 7 or 8 scenes per session, so it adds up quickly. And they're Hunters, so they also get plenty of Practical Experience.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1274,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","user":"Crazy_Ivan","date":". 10-15-2015, 09:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1274-crazy_ivan","name":"Crazy_Ivan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1274_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}